      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To calculate the straight-line depreciation, you'll need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of depreciation periods, which in this case is the useful life of the machine (8 years).\n2. Divide the cost of the machine ($145,000) by the total number of depreciation periods (8 years).\n3. This will give you the annual depreciation expense, which you can then subtract from the cost of the machine.\n4. In this case, the annual depreciation expense would be $145,000 / 8 years = $18,125 per year.\n5. As a check, make sure the annual accumulation of depreciation in the book and on the financial statement matches the pathways for the total cost through the straight-line method.\n\nThis ensures a consistent and accurate depreciation schedule that's in line with your company's accounting policies.",
